# gb (2026-11-25) = fw (the only recipe that learned to walk: forward only) + the night fixes: critic reads the command, long segments, stall on sequences, and the sequence progress ratchet at the goal tiles weight (60) so every direction gets the pay that taught fw forward.
# gd = gb (with CRITIC_CMD) resumed actor-only from fw model_3000 (MJLAB_LOAD_ACTOR_ONLY=1, fresh critic that reads the command): gc 3250 (same without CRITIC_CMD) walked forward 0.98 and nothing else, as fz.
# ge = gd + MJLAB_CRITIC_WARMUP=100 (actor frozen for the first 100 updates): gd model_0, i.e. fw 3000 after ONE update with the fresh critic (weights moved ~0.005), fell 12/16 on a forward command where fw 3000 fell 1/16.
# gf = ge + lr held at 1e-3 during the 100-update critic warm-up, then MJLAB_RESUME_LR 1e-5 (fw ended at 1e-5): ge, warm-up with the adaptive schedule, climbed to lr 1e-2 (KL 0 with a frozen actor) and collapsed at the unfreeze (episode 841 -> 259 steps).
